      "value": "Thought it was about time for an update.\nSo I finished weight-painting the upper chest, and as I thought, it did not help.\nI also realized that in testing, I wore my hip tracker on the right side of my hip, instead of in the front or back, and I *thought* that I fixed it by moving the hip tracker to the back, but I have yet to reproduce the proper behavior afterwards. I assume I was accidentally on a different build of VRChat, which is what allowed the bending.\nIn essence, it is broken no matter where the hip tracker is located. \nAnother update is I got 4 3.0 trackers for 10 point tracking, which also has the bending problem (not that I thought more trackers would help this specific case).\nTo be clear, I tested everything using both 6 and 10 point tracking.\nI don't know if there is any other useful information for resolving this, although I am willing to do whatever is needed to test.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
